{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779395076,"nonce":"739LJ4nhgKIIzLBFDsvB8/V1iOY=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDBUH9w","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/150","origin":"github"},"title":"Post-deployment data analysis: 2026-05-21 OTH + FCU reconfig deployment (#149 follow-up)","message":"## Parent\n\nPart of [#149](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/149) (2026-05-21 deployment). Bag review couldn't happen on the day — most of the validation matrix moved to offline analysis after the trackline was rejected by an unhealthy nav stack and the OTH segment ended with a collision-driven early recovery.\n\n## Bag locations\n\n- Boat: `~/data/logs/bizzyboat/` — sessions starting `2026-05-21T12:16:53` (pre-launch) and `2026-05-21T13:11:08` (mid-mission). Multiple sessions; the second likely starts after a nav-stack-related restart.\n- Operator: `~/data/logs/operator/`\n- Sonar (M3): `~/data/logs/bizzyboat_sonar/`\n- Analysis outputs land in `~/data/logs/analysis/` per convention.\n\n## Scope — seven topics\n\nFor each topic: read bag → answer the question → write a short report into `~/data/logs/analysis/2026-05-21/\u003ctopic\u003e.md`. If a topic gets deep, file a sub-issue referencing this one and move detailed work there.\n\n### 1. #138 closure validation — `mavros/global_position/global` vs SBG\n\nDid today's FCU reconfig (`EK3_SRC1_POSZ=3` + `EK3_GPS_OFFS_{X,Y,Z}`) actually deliver `/global` Z at `base_link` with chart-datum-compatible behavior?\n\n- [ ] Static agreement: `/bizzy/mavros/global_position/global` Z vs `/bizzy/sensors/sbg/gps_pos` Z (with undulation applied) at a stationary moment\n- [ ] Stability over minute-scale: the prior known failure mode is ~5 m/hr drift on `/global` with `EK3_SRC1_POSZ=1` (baro). Look for this drift in the OTH window; absence = reconfig delivered\n- [ ] Body-frame `SBG − MAV` offset: should drop toward GPS-CEP (sub-decimeter), not the 0.64 m steady offset documented in [#111](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/111)\n- [ ] If all three pass, **#138 can be closed**.\n\n### 2. `udp_bridge#24` WARN demote validation\n\nDid the WARN demote actually deliver against the 2026-05-19 baseline?\n\n- [ ] Count `Giving up on resend` WARN events in `/rosout` over the OTH window. Compare to **27,992 events in 2 hours** baseline from 2026-05-19.\n- [ ] Per-remote `DiagnosticStatus` from the demote PR: read `/bizzy/udp_bridge/diagnostics` and tabulate give-up rate per remote.\n- [ ] Confound to characterize: today the M3 sonar was streaming during the OTH window (changed mid-mission per dev log 13:19) — baseline was lower-bandwidth. Note in the report; may need to bracket comparison with sonar-on vs sonar-off segments if both exist.\n\n### 3. Bandwidth / Starlink saturation during OTH\n\nPer [`#149` Phase 5 stretch](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/149) and the roadmap \"must finish before June 4\" budget cull:\n\n- [ ] Plot uplink bandwidth in the OTH window (Starlink-only). Throughput, packet loss, saturation events.\n- [ ] Identify which topics dominate the budget. Note M3 sonar's share since it was streaming.\n- [ ] If saturation events correlate with `udp_bridge` give-up events from topic 2, note that.\n\n### 4. Collision incident reconstruction\n\nThe central question raised by the incident at ~13:57 EDT: was this a **perception gap** (costmap didn't see the floating platform) or an **autonomy gap** (BT planner ignored the costmap on return-to-line)?\n\n- [ ] Pull `/bizzy/local_costmap/costmap` in the 30 seconds before impact (recording was added today via `a06f38a`).\n- [ ] Inspect OAK forward camera segmentation in the same window — was the platform classified as non-water/obstacle?\n- [ ] Cross-check BT navigator's published path / `lookahead_point` against the costmap data: did it have a free-cost path that ran through the platform?\n- [ ] If costmap missed the platform → perception gap (floating-platform recognition is a class-day hazard).\n- [ ] If costmap had it but BT planned through → autonomy gap (path replan after manual override doesn't fully respect inflation).\n\n### 5. Battery voltage trend across the uncharged day\n\nBoat was launched with uncharged batteries intentionally; today doubles as a draw-down observation.\n\n- [ ] Plot `/bizzy/mavros/battery` voltage across the whole session (boat-on time, not just on-water).\n- [ ] Compare today's starting voltage to yesterday's tail-end voltage from `~/data/logs/bizzyboat/` 2026-05-20 session (the boat was on for a few hours yesterday without deployment).\n- [ ] Note any voltage knees or rapid drops correlated with mission events (collision, sonar-on, OTH transit, etc.).\n\n### 6. Phase 0/1 nav stack unhealthy — root cause\n\nAt ~13:28 EDT a trackline launch was rejected because the nav stack wasn't healthy. Multiple plausible causes:\n\n- [ ] Were `controller_server`, `planner_server`, `bt_navigator` all in `active` lifecycle state? Check transition_event topics or service queries in the bag.\n- [ ] Was `bizzy/map → bizzy/map_tide` TF resolved at the time? (This was the #135 root cause — re-occurrence is plausible.)\n- [ ] Were there ERROR/WARN entries in `~/.ros/log/\u003csession\u003e/` from `controller_server` (especially `sea_surface_layer` matchSize, given the multi-instance segfault discovered today)?\n- [ ] Most likely-cause-rank hypothesis going in: **multi-instance `sea_surface_layer` segfault was already crashing `controller_server` before the trackline attempt** — the per-layer crash mode would prevent lifecycle activation. PR [`seafloor_echoboat_project11#21`](https://github.com/rolker/seafloor_echoboat_project11/pull/21)'s forward-only workaround should make this go away on the next deployment; verify by checking the rebuilt costmap layers in the bag right before / during the rejection.\n\n### 7. `mru_transform` `/global` switch validation\n\nField commit `f348f66` switched `mru_transform` from `mavros/global_position/raw/fix` (the 2026-05-19 field workaround) back to `mavros/global_position/global`. Confirm this switch held cleanly through the rest of the deployment.\n\n- [ ] Find the commit-time-equivalent moment in the bag (or by `/rosout` event for `mru_transform` reconfigure).\n- [ ] After the switch: does `/bizzy/tide_estimate` stay in the chart-datum plausibility band?\n- [ ] Any new `sea_surface_estimator` suppression warnings post-switch?\n- [ ] If clean, then **the field-revert from 2026-05-19 (`c36acfa`) is fully undone**; if `tide_estimate` goes out of band post-switch, we have new information about the FCU reconfig that contradicts topic 1's finding.\n\n## Anti-scope\n\nThis issue collects findings; it doesn't ship code or config changes. If an analysis topic surfaces a needed code change, file a focused issue against the relevant repo and reference this one. Same for ADR-level questions or roadmap entries.\n\n## Wrap-up condition\n\nIssue closes when all 7 topic checkboxes are addressed (either in this issue's appended reports, or in linked sub-issues if any topic went deep).\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}